From: Seeed Rockchip BSP
Subject: [PATCH] fiq_debugger: keep the console alive on serial break

The RK FIQ debugger console treats a received serial BREAK (line error,
as generated by some USB serial adapters when the host toggles DTR while
opening the port) as a request to enter the debugger command interpreter:
it clears console_enable, prints "Welcome to irq debugger" and from then
on all input is consumed by the debug> prompt instead of the tty.  For a
device whose only console is ttyFIQ0 this makes the serial console
unusable until someone types the "console" debugger command.

Only honor the break entry when the console passthrough is already off,
so a stray break can never steal the console from getty/login.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/fiq_debugger/fiq_debugger.c	2026-08-27 16:12:08.220544302 +0800
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/fiq_debugger/fiq_debugger.c	2026-08-27 16:12:08.237434285 +0800
@@ -945,7 +945,7 @@
 				state->debug_count = 0;
 				fiq_debugger_prompt(state);
 			}
-		} else if (c == FIQ_DEBUGGER_BREAK) {
+		} else if (c == FIQ_DEBUGGER_BREAK && !state->console_enable) {
 			state->console_enable = false;
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP
 			fiq_debugger_puts(state, "\nWelcome to ");
